    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d718">

                <pb facs="0742" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/1234: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-09-06T17:00:00+08:00">September 6, 1932—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 6—6:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1074. My 1058, September 3, 1 p.m. Following from Cunningham: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 6, 9 a.m. Legation’s July 30, 2 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                                >1?</hi>] p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d718-f1"/> paragraph 1, last
                            sentence. Notwithstanding various complications which have arisen as
                            reported in my August 31 [<hi rendition="#italic">13?</hi>], 10 a.m.,
                            and previous telegrams it is assumed that foregoing instruction is still
                            in effect.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>To which I have replied: “Views expressed in my July 30, 1 p.m., still
                    stand.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d718-f1" n="3" xml:id="d718-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 961, August 16, 1932, 7 p.m., from the Minister in China, <ref
                        target="#pg635">p. 635</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
